We can rewrite that question as an equation.

$\begin{array}{ccccc}
\greenD{6\,\text{km}}&\text{is}&\blueD{75\%}&\text{of}&\purpleD{\text{what distance}}\\\\
\greenD{6}&=&\blueD{0.75}&\times&\purpleD{?}
\end{array}$

Let's solve for the unknown distance.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{\greenD{6}}{0.75}&=\dfrac{\blueD{0.75}\times\purpleD{?}}{0.75}\\\\
\purpleD{8}&=\purpleD{?}
\end{align}$

Haruka hiked $\purpleD{8\,\text{km}}$ in the morning and $\greenD{6\,\text{km}}$ in the afternoon. How far did she hike in all?
